    "body": "### Problem\n\n`:restart` leaves `'winminwidth'` and `'winminheight'` set to `0` after restoring a session with split windows across multiple tabpages.\n\nThis seems to happen when multiple tabpages each contain split windows. The split direction does not appear to matter.\n\nIt looks like the restart/session restore path temporarily sets these options to `0` while restoring the window layout, but does not restore them afterwards for this layout.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate `repro_winmin.vim`:\n\n```vim\nsp\ntabe\nsp\nrestart set winminwidth? winminheight?\n```\n\nThen run:\n\n```sh\nnvim --clean\n```\n\nInside Nvim:\n\n```vim\n:source repro_winmin.vim\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`'winminwidth'` and `'winminheight'` should not be left at `0` after `:restart`.\n\nThey should retain their normal/default values, or at least the temporary values used during session/window layout restoration should not leak into the restarted instance.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nAfter `:restart`, the following is shown:\n\n```vim\nwinminwidth=0\nwinminheight=0\n```\n\n### Additional context\n\nThis appears to be related to the automatic session/window layout restoration done by `:restart`.\nA single tabpage with splits does not appear to trigger the same result.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-866+g62c0984647\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nUbuntu 26.04\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\ngnome-terminal\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
